WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.300
Bad writing, a perpetual victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.134
and a shifting role. Why do fans want&nbsp;
Yellowstone creators to kill off Monica?

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.600
To be a member of the Dutton family in&nbsp;
Yellowstone is to spend your life defending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.700
your physical and mental real estate. However,&nbsp;
there are exceptions to the ruthless streak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.480
that runs in the members of the rancher&nbsp;
family. Having married into the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.460
Monica Dutton tends to be more level-headed than&nbsp;
pretty much any other character bearing the name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.680
Though she goes through her own crises — both in&nbsp;
her relationship with Kayce and otherwise — she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.300
generally the most sensible person in any&nbsp;
given room that contains multiple Duttons.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.820
Unfortunately for Monica, comparatively normal&nbsp;
people aren't necessarily the most popular ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.040
in their shows, especially when said shows tend&nbsp;
to focus around ruthless people who operate in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.500
an extremely gray moral area. While viewers have&nbsp;
been moved by some scenes, it appears that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.420
goodwill toward this gentler character isn't&nbsp;
eternal. Have the events surrounding the death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.400
of Monica and Kayce's child and the former's&nbsp;
growing discontent with the Dutton ranch caused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.320
some viewers to turn on the character, or is there&nbsp;
some underlying reason behind their animosity?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.810
Let's take a look at the reason Yellowstone&nbsp;
fans are losing their patience with Monica.

00:01:12.348 --> 00:01:16.320
Monica's reservations toward the&nbsp;
Dutton lifestyle might be reasonable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.160
but the show's approach to the character&nbsp;
seems to have started rubbing some fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.280
the wrong way. In Yellowstone Season 5 Episode&nbsp;
4, Horses in Heaven, the character experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.380
one of the worst days of her life, as she&nbsp;
undergoes a ceremony to bury her baby. Fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.520
have even been getting emotional over Monica's&nbsp;
tender moment with John Dutton, in which the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.440
no-nonsense Dutton patriarch takes some time&nbsp;
to comfort Monica with choice words of wisdom.

00:01:40.571 --> 00:01:45.180
"All he knew was you, and that you loved him."

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.640
For some viewers, however, Monica's constant&nbsp;
turmoil isn't quite so moving. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.500
Season 5 viewers have noted that Monica has become&nbsp;
the show's go-to character for sympathy points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.820
while also being off-puttingly critical of&nbsp;
the Dutton lifestyle. One person tweeted,

00:02:07.272 --> 00:02:12.600
Instead of taking affront with any specific&nbsp;
action Monica has done in the show, it appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:18.840
that in some corners of the fandom she's built a&nbsp;
reputation as a generally annoying character — at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.920
least, going by the online reaction she's&nbsp;
been getting during her Season 5 appearances.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.180
One fan tweeted,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.460
Another viewer tweeted,

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:40.440
Elsewhere, another viewer said&nbsp;
something similar, writing,

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:48.060
While Monica has given fans many&nbsp;
heartwarming moments over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.660
it appears that at least some viewers&nbsp;
have grown tired of her. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.140
Monica's smaller Season 5 role has&nbsp;
some fans worried for her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:00.480
so whether you love the character or dislike her,&nbsp;
it's an interesting time to be a Yellowstone fan.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.149
"Thank you."

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.240
In an interview with KCRW, Professor&nbsp;
Tressie McMillan Cottom pointed out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.720
how Yellowstone attempts to chip away&nbsp;
at the mythology of the American West.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.468
Cottom told the station,

00:03:17.478 --> 00:03:20.580
This is an accurate assessment&nbsp;
of the series' better intentions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.660
particularly in Seasons 1 and 2,&nbsp;
when both the tribal narrative and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.720
Monica and Kayce's relationship&nbsp;
played a less superficial role.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.980
"Can't afford a different ranch."

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.060
"I don't think you can afford&nbsp;
to stay on this one, in here."

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:41.580
But McMillan Cottom's word choice is revealing.&nbsp;
The racial diversity is "cosmetic," and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.860
Native American cast is "well," not "fully,"&nbsp;
fleshed out. And the show's move away from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.280
central narrative that highlighted the&nbsp;
Duttons' tension with other Montanans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.180
has been accompanied by a disregarding of&nbsp;
Monica's relevance and meaning in the story.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.340
At the outset, Monica had a job. Monica had&nbsp;
a degree. Monica was supposedly integral in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.940
highlighting — as Taylor Sheridan&nbsp;
happily boasts in an interview with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.840
the Atlantic — "the way Native American&nbsp;
women were treated." Most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.740
Monica was meant to be Kayce's equal, a&nbsp;
partner who kept him from turning to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:14.071
Dutton dark side, rather than&nbsp;
an obstacle to his happiness.

00:04:14.134 --> 00:04:17.014
"Number one, I make more&nbsp;
money than you do, cowboy."

00:04:17.014 --> 00:04:23.220
In Season 5, Monica only exists to highlight&nbsp;
the torn Kayce's role as The Good Dutton. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.300
Heroic Cowboy decision to choose her&nbsp;
is the sole reason for her existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:32.161
a writing decision with indefensible&nbsp;
implications and disastrous consequences.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.380
Given the show's baffling move away&nbsp;
from treating Monica as a whole human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.180
it's genuinely hard not to wonder if a&nbsp;
certain contingent of the series' fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.020
didn't influence the writing. Because the&nbsp;
Monica we're following at this point is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.560
far away from the Monica we met at the&nbsp;
beginning of the series, and not in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.420
good way. In response to fans pleading for the&nbsp;
series to kill Monica, Dustin Rowles writes,

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:21.480
As a soap opera in contemporary western&nbsp;
clothing, one expects a certain degree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.280
of tragedy and melodrama, but it’s only Monica&nbsp;
who's yet to reap the narrative benefit of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:32.040
experiences in the form of a display of strength,&nbsp;
revenge, or lessons learned. Were Monica written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:36.600
to exemplify a different kind of strength,&nbsp;
or to stand in contrast to Beth's volatility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:41.700
that might redeem some of her suffering.&nbsp;
But as it stands, Monica's pain serves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.860
as Indie Wire’s Kristen Lopez notes, to make&nbsp;
viewers recoil at the tragedy of it all.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:52.260
It's a curious use of the character, considering&nbsp;
just how many viewers have grown tired of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.300
exploitation, and so much so that they're willing&nbsp;
to blame the character, or even the actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:03.600
for low-hanging fruit writing. Monica is, indeed&nbsp;
— as many of her haters point out — a perpetual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:09.660
victim. But Monica is also a fictional character.&nbsp;
She exists because she was written. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:14.160
she really doesn't exist the way the other&nbsp;
characters do because of how she is written.

